WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.269
That night Mowgli stayed with Messua in her hut.

2
00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:10.131
As they ate dinner, she told him that her husband had died.

3
00:00:10.132 --> 00:00:13.185
"But you saved our lives that night, Mowgli."

4
00:00:13.186 --> 00:00:17.532
Her eyes filled with grateful tears.

5
00:00:17.533 --> 00:00:20.368
"And we have had a good life here.

6
00:00:20.369 --> 00:00:30.243
There's a village nearby, and I am content."

7
00:00:30.244 --> 00:00:35.216
In the morning Mowgli got ready to go.

8
00:00:35.217 --> 00:00:39.801
"Please visit again," Messua whispered, hugging him.

9
00:00:39.802 --> 00:00:42.121
"I love you."

10
00:00:42.122 --> 00:00:44.694
Mowgli's throat felt tight.

11
00:00:44.695 --> 00:00:47.284
"I love you too, Messua.

12
00:00:47.285 --> 00:00:53.110
And I will come back soon. I promise."

13
00:00:53.111 --> 00:00:58.851
As he headed toward the marsh, a large beast jumped out of the tall grass.

14
00:00:58.852 --> 00:01:02.646
"Bagheera!" Mowgli said in surprise.

15
00:01:02.647 --> 00:01:05.474
"What are you doing here?"

16
00:01:05.475 --> 00:01:08.690
"I followed you," Bagheera replied.

17
00:01:08.691 --> 00:01:14.482
"Again?" Mowgli laughed and shook his head.

18
00:01:14.483 --> 00:01:17.023
"You're always following me.

19
00:01:17.024 --> 00:01:20.485
So are Mother Wolf and Gray Brother."

20
00:01:20.486 --> 00:01:23.138
Bagheera looked nervous.

21
00:01:23.139 --> 00:01:27.652
"Are you . . . Are you coming back to the jungle?" he asked.

22
00:01:27.653 --> 00:01:31.704
"I . . . I thought you might stay here with the woman."

23
00:01:31.705 --> 00:01:33.933
Mowgli shook his head.

24
00:01:33.934 --> 00:01:38.919
"I don't think I belong with people, Bagheera.

25
00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:44.663
The man pack threw me out—remember? Just like the wolf pack."

26
00:01:44.664 --> 00:01:48.585
Bagheera studied Mowgli for a second.

27
00:01:48.586 --> 00:01:54.112
Then he lifted his chin. "Feel under my jaw."

28
00:01:54.113 --> 00:01:58.834
Mowgli obediently put his fingers under Bagheera's silky chin.

29
00:01:58.835 --> 00:02:02.488
The panther's fur covered thick muscles.

30
00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:08.709
Then Mowgli touched a bare patch. "What's this?" he asked.

31
00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:13.242
"It is the mark of a collar," Bagheera said.

32
00:02:13.243 --> 00:02:20.660
"No one in the jungle knows this—I was also born among people, Mowgli.

33
00:02:20.661 --> 00:02:23.757
I lived in a cage at the king's palace."

34
00:02:23.758 --> 00:02:27.545
"What?" Mowgli blinked in surprise.

35
00:02:27.546 --> 00:02:31.086
Bagheera had lived with humans too?

36
00:02:31.087 --> 00:02:37.584
"That's why I spoke for you at the council when you were a little cub," Bagheera went on.

37
00:02:37.585 --> 00:02:40.845
"My mother died in the cages at the palace.

38
00:02:40.846 --> 00:02:45.585
After that, I had no family there, and . . ."

39
00:02:45.586 --> 00:02:51.075
Mowgli couldn't imagine the beautiful, strong panther trapped in a cage.

40
00:02:51.076 --> 00:02:54.743
"The cage must have felt like prison."

41
00:02:54.744 --> 00:02:59.030
"It was a prison," Bagheera said.

42
00:02:59.031 --> 00:03:02.801
"I lived there without ever seeing the jungle.

43
00:03:02.802 --> 00:03:07.187
Then one night I mysteriously found my strength.

44
00:03:07.188 --> 00:03:11.887
I told myself I was a panther—not a plaything for people.

45
00:03:11.888 --> 00:03:16.395
And I broke the silly lock with one blow of my paw."

46
00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:22.310
Mowgli grinned. That was something he could picture Bagheera doing.

47
00:03:22.311 --> 00:03:25.171
"Now you know my secret, Little Brother.

48
00:03:25.172 --> 00:03:28.311
I returned to the jungle where I belonged.

49
00:03:28.312 --> 00:03:32.308
As for you . . ." Bagheera paused.

50
00:03:32.309 --> 00:03:34.043
"You are a human.

51
00:03:34.044 --> 00:03:38.793
So one day you too will return to where you belong."

52
00:03:38.794 --> 00:03:41.952
"Nope. Sorry, Bagheera, but you're wrong."

53
00:03:41.953 --> 00:03:44.586
Mowgli shook his head firmly.

54
00:03:44.587 --> 00:03:47.752
"I won't ever live with people again.

55
00:03:47.753 --> 00:03:54.323
I'll visit Messua, but that's about it."

56
00:03:54.324 --> 00:03:56.398
He patted the panther.

57
00:03:56.399 --> 00:04:02.276
"And when I'm older and on my own, I'll come back to visit you and Baloo—"

58
00:04:02.277 --> 00:04:08.106
Just then a girl in a flowing white dress appeared on the path.

59
00:04:08.107 --> 00:04:11.908
Mowgli and Bagheera ducked behind some bushes.

60
00:04:11.909 --> 00:04:16.827
As the girl passed, Mowgli moved the bushes with his hand.

61
00:04:16.828 --> 00:04:24.196
He watched the girl walk toward the marsh.

62
00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:30.094
"The boy is both man and wolf," Bagheera thought, watching him tenderly.

63
00:04:30.095 --> 00:04:35.461
"But one day he will become more man than wolf."

64
00:04:35.462 --> 00:04:40.995
The girl disappeared, and Bagheera nudged Mowgli with his nose.

65
00:04:40.996 --> 00:04:44.097
"Ready to go home, Little Brother?"

66
00:04:44.098 --> 00:04:48.690
"Yes." Mowgli leaped onto the panther's back.

67
00:04:48.691 --> 00:05:00.362
Then together they went back into the jungle.

